# Verification routes

Use this page only after the project has more than one executable product-verification route or an operator procedure worth indexing.

A route proves one behavior through **Surface, Run, Drive, Observe, Isolate**: its public interface, readiness and launch, caller action, distinguishing result or side effect, and owned cleanup. A green build or test process alone is not evidence for a user journey.

Automated routes live in `.harness/verification.toml` and point to executable scripts under `scripts/verify/`. `mise run verify` runs matching required routes in CI; use `scripts/verify-routes --path <changed-path>` during focused work. A route without a selector runs all required routes.

Keep manual or credentialed checks out of the registry. Record their operator steps, actual observation, and limitations in validation evidence instead of calling them automated passes.
